  "markdown_report": "**Recommendation:** proceed with matched-target prefix-removal training in the supplied corrected GRU4Rec. At 10% progress, this controlled experiment offers a clearer next step than learned history selection; no validation improvement has been established.\n\n**Insights from the starting point.** (1) Latest padding probes pass across all four categories, with maximum state error below 7.1×10⁻⁷ and unchanged probe top-10 lists. This supports numerical consistency on tested layouts, without establishing universal invariance. (2) Electronics has 8.25% sampled wrong-rank positions and 19.81% margins below 0.5. These identify training weaknesses, not validation performance or harmful older context. (3) Feedback suggests that broad historical affinity sometimes misses immediate choice. Ownership, compatibility and latent intent remain unobserved, so recency is a hypothesis to test.\n\n**Insights from related work.** (1) FCESR and Demystifying Sequential Recommendations motivate separating history sufficiency from necessity [1,2]. Deletion sensitivity can reveal dependence without establishing predictive harm. (2) TimeSHAP and Does It Look Sequential? motivate recurrent-history interventions [3,4]. Their diagnostic precedents do not establish that cropped training will improve this task. (3) Krichene and Rendle show limitations of sampled ranking metrics [5]. Preserve host HR@10 for selection while clearly distinguishing training audits from generalization.\n\nThese insights organize three directions: trustworthy encoding, controlled context interventions, and ranking-aware diagnosis. The framework separates intervention location from supervision:\n\n| Condition | Training context | Supervised positions | Interpretation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | Full | All valid | Baseline |\n| B | Full | Sampled suffix | Supervision control |\n| C | Same sampled suffix | Identical to B | Context intervention |\n\n**Candidate ideas.** Scores are originality/potential/difficulty; higher difficulty means harder implementation.\n\n| Idea | Scores | Positive assessment | Negative assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Matched-target prefix removal [1–3] | 4/7/5 | Feasible; separates context from supervision | Familiar augmentation; residual stochastic differences |\n| Frozen prefix/recent/random deletion audit [1–4] | 3/6/3 | Cheap comparison of context dependence | Perturbations can create atypical histories |\n| Jointly learned GRU forgetting gate | 5/7/7 | Adaptive retention within one network | Adds capacity and weakens attribution |\n\n**Selected algorithm.** On a probability-0.5 branch, retain K uniformly sampled from ceil(n/2)…n chronological real inputs; otherwise retain all n. B and C share retained positions, original next-item targets, negatives, initialization and schedules. B retains connected prefix gradients; C zeros the removed prefix. Preserve causal target alignment and normalize the actual baseline objective consistently over retained supervision.\n\n```text\nsample baseline batch and candidate pool\nconstruct suffix mask using independent crop RNG\ncontext = cropped input for C; full input for A/B\nsupervision = all valid for A; retained valid for B/C\nupdate one GRU using unchanged baseline objective\n```\n\nUse full-history inference and final-nonpadding readout. Compare complete conditions only if all twelve category fits fit the remaining shared budget; select by macro validation HR@10, without fusion. Preserve seeds, routing, diagnostic interfaces and predictor consistency. C−B measures this training intervention, not stale intent. References [1–5] appear in related_work.",
  "idea": {
    "description": "Test stochastic old-prefix removal in the supplied corrected GRU4Rec using a matched-target full-context control. Execute each condition as a separate trial with one independently trained model per category, and deploy one complete selected condition with exactly one checkpoint per category.",
    "motivation": "The latest supplied diagnostics pass padding calibration in all four categories with both TF32 flags disabled, making further extensive numerical debugging unnecessary unless new failures appear. Qualitative feedback motivates a recency hypothesis, while sampled training margins—particularly Electronics' 8.25% wrong-rank rate—do not establish harmful older context or validation gains. At 10% progress, isolating context changes from supervision changes is more informative than introducing adaptive selectors.",
    "implementation_notes": "Integrate into the host-supplied corrected baseline; its architecture, sampler and objective are not supplied here and must not be reconstructed from assumptions. Retain the GRU4Rec backbone and any jointly trained baseline readout. A uses full context and all valid supervision; B uses full context with suffix supervision; C removes the prefix and uses exactly B's supervision. Preserve connected gradients through B's prefix.\n\nFor each nonempty row, let n be its real-input count. With probability 0.5 draw K uniformly from max(1,ceil(n/2)) through n inclusive; otherwise K=n. Retain the final K real-input positions, with singleton rows unchanged. Actual removal probability is below 0.5 because K=n is allowed. Preserve original aligned positive and negative targets; never reconnect targets across deleted positions. Keep inference on full permitted histories.\n\nMatch B/C initialization, base batches, crop plans, candidate IDs, multiplicities, filtering and sampling corrections using independent deterministic RNG streams. Construct coupled candidate pools before supervision masking. Preserve the actual objective's semantics: use a retained-position mean only where the baseline objective admits that decomposition, match positionwise regularization, and retain global regularization. Do not introduce sampling corrections or additional negative-count normalization. Handle empty supervised batches identically and record actual updates. Different recurrent execution paths may still change dropout masks; do not claim identical stochastic trajectories.\n\nUse the existing successful precision protocol as a bounded regression check, preserving its declared tolerances and restoring diagnostic settings afterward. Do not infer universal invariance from the supplied small probe. Compact chronological real tokens before any packed recurrence, restore aligned B×L×H features, and gather the greatest nonpadding position rather than count-1. Define empty-history behavior explicitly.\n\nPredeclare a common epoch count no greater than 200, exactly 200 batches per epoch, final-epoch checkpoints, validation-query cap and timing allocation. Respect the SASREC_EPOCHS default of 200 despite its name. All twelve category-condition fits, diagnostics and failures share the remaining 43,200 GPU-second budget; four slots do not multiply it. If affordability is unknown or insufficient, report the comparison as incomplete rather than claiming matched evidence. Each separate trial trains only its chosen condition's four category models on one GPU. Never inspect other trials or reuse their checkpoints.\n\nSelect one complete condition using equal-weight macro validation HR@10; predeclare exact ties as A, then B, then C. Preserve the pinned evaluator: 200 validation users/category, 99 unique negatives and evaluation seed 42. Report C−B and B−A separately, with category scores and retained-supervision counts. If per-user hits are exposed, paired within-category bootstrap intervals may supplement aggregate results; otherwise mark them unavailable. Such intervals exclude training-seed variation and adaptive-selection bias. No held-out improvement is currently established.\n\nKeep preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four category routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and trial-local artifacts. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), family-specific sample_batch and every ModelView interface. Accept (None, sequence, positive, negative) with B×L tensors; restore model mode even on failure and return measured metrics plus definitions. Use only permitted histories, titles, descriptions and timestamps; unavailable ratings, reviews, ownership, compatibility and simulator traits must remain unavailable. Preserve unseen-item full-catalog recommendations for twenty training users, five/category.\n\nUpdate the predictor writer whenever inference changes. Strictly reload the saved architecture and exactly one checkpoint/category, then compare generated-predictor scores against the training-side model on identical histories and candidates. Do not average checkpoints, mix category winners across conditions or combine independent scores. The code has not been executed or evaluated in this writing call.",
    "pseudocode": "Predeclare conditions A/B/C, crop probability 0.5, common E<=200,\n200 batches/epoch, final checkpoints, query cap, tie order and charged budget.\nCheck affordability of twelve category-condition fits from host accounting.\n\nFor each separately executed condition:\n  For each of the four required categories:\n    initialize supplied corrected GRU4Rec with training seed 42\n    initialize reproducible independent sampling and crop streams\n    For epoch in range(E):\n      For batch_index in range(200):\n        _, x, positive, negative = family_specific_sample_batch(...)\n        candidates = baseline_candidate_pool_before_masking(...)\n        keep = false mask shaped like x\n        For each nonempty row:\n          positions = chronological nonpadding positions\n          n = number of positions\n          K = n\n          if crop_rng.random() < 0.5:\n            K = uniform_integer(max(1, ceil(n/2)), n)\n          keep[row, positions[-K:]] = True\n        valid = baseline_valid_supervision(x, positive, negative)\n        context = x.masked_fill(~keep, 0) if condition == C else x\n        supervision = valid if condition == A else valid & keep\n        features = model.log2feats(context)\n        loss = actual_baseline_objective(features, original_targets,\n                 fixed_candidates, supervision, declared_reduction)\n        update using baseline optimizer and schedule\n        log retained counts, actual updates and charged time\n    save final checkpoint and matching predictor artifacts\n    verify finite outputs, final-nonpadding readout and strict reload\n    compare training-side and generated-predictor scores\n  obtain unchanged host macro validation HR@10\n\nReport C-B and B-A only for completed matched conditions.\nSelect one complete condition by macro HR@10; ties prefer A/B/C.\nDeploy full-history inference with one checkpoint per category and no fusion.\nPreserve diagnosis adapter and all ModelView interfaces.",
    "originality": {
      "score": 4,
      "positive": "Matched suffix supervision and fixed candidate construction make a familiar cropping intervention more interpretable.",
      "negative": "History deletion, recurrent augmentation and controlled ablations already have substantial precedent."
